<title>USA: SunTrust Banks sells $350 mln in notes.</title>
<headline>SunTrust Banks sells $350 mln in notes.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-05-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following issue of floating rates notes from SunTrust Banks Inc was priced on Monday, according to lead manager Lehman Brothers Inc.</p>
<p>The offering was increased in size to $350 million from an original size of $300 million.</p>
<p>BORROWER SUNTRUST BANKS INC</p>
<p>AMT $350 MLN	 COUPON 3MO LIBOR +67 MATURITY 5/15/2027</p>
<p>TYPE FLT RATE NTS  ISS PRICE 99.313     FIRST PAY DATE 8/15/97</p>
<p>LAST MOODY'S A1    YIELD 3MO LIBOR +73  PAY FREQ  QUARTERLY</p>
<p>LAST S&amp;P A-MINUS				CALLABLE NON-CALL TEN</p>
<p>((--U.S. Corporate Bond Unit, 212 859-1678))</p>
</text>
